WEBVTT

00:07:59.371 --> 00:08:03.621
So I'll start at the question of who
becomes a leader versus who's

00:08:03.621 --> 00:08:06.246
an effective leader. So one
of the things we find over

00:08:06.246 --> 00:08:09.454
and over again in my world of
organizational psychology is that

00:08:09.454 --> 00:08:12.704
the individuals that we elevate
to leadership roles are often

00:08:12.704 --> 00:08:17.079
the most narcissistic, selfish takers
because they show dominance and strength.

00:08:17.454 --> 00:08:21.913
But that ultimately, when we look at who
leads well and and both inspires people

00:08:21.913 --> 00:08:25.246
and guides a group toward achieving
a common goal most productively,

00:08:25.829 --> 00:08:28.913
it tends much more to be the humble,
other oriented,

00:08:28.913 --> 00:08:31.871
generous givers who are willing
to put the team or